Dealing with the wizard the first time you meet him is not really hard.
*You* determine the conditions of that encounter. I normally kill all
the eels in his moat before and freeze all of the moat. Still, the hell
hound that is with him will almost always manage to unfreeze a square,
so I pay attention not to kill the wizard over water, even though I know
that the bug that made me lose the Book of the Dead in my first
would-be-ascension (it fell into the moat, which I froze to retrieve it,
but it was gone) has meanwhile been removed.

In nethack, I would use a wand of death, which should work after a few
tries. In slash'em, I send him 7 +4 or +5 bullets using an assault
rifle, which usually kills him in one turn. Otherwise, I just repeat.

The advantage of getting him out of his tower is that you can retreat to
the staircase, which allows you to kill him in melee, if your wand of
death does not work as expected. If your quest artifact provides magic
resistance, that might be a useful approach. The same effect might be
achieved with a cursed potion of gain level quaffed in the wizard's
tower when he is not next to you. Then you can come downstairs a few
turns later. (Would that work, i.e. can you move up through the ceiling
from the wizard's tower?)


